                <pb facs="0930" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg824"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Memorandum.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Foreign
                            Affairs to Minister Combs.</hi></head>
                <p>The secretary of state and of the department for foreign affairs of the republic
                    of Guatemala has the honor to salute his excellency Mr. Minister Plenipotentiary
                    of the United States of America and returns the telegrams of Messrs. Kensett
                    Champney &amp; Co., which to-day he has transcribed to the minister of public
                    works, begging him that they be no further molested in the matter of
                    laborers.</p>
                <p>Juan Barrios M. avails himself of this opportunity to renew to Mr. Combs,
                    etc.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-05-07"><hi rendition="#small-caps">May</hi> 7,
                        1906</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
